## To finish the enrichment (one call, once Enrichr is reachable)
```bash
pip install gseapy && python3 /workspace/analysis/run_enrichment.py
# conservative DE list, to see how the DE core's liberalness moves the OR:
python3 /workspace/analysis/run_enrichment.py --gene-list /workspace/analysis/de_symbols_t_df4.txt
# optional, only if gseapy imports and you supply the library; output is labelled APPROXIMATION:
python3 /workspace/analysis/run_enrichment.py --local-gmt /path/to/Reactome_2022.gmt
```
The headline answer is the Odds Ratio for the **1,680-symbol (raw-p) list**, per the agreed protocol;
the t(df=4) run is the robustness check, not the answer.
It runs `gseapy.enrich(gene_list=<1680 symbols>, gene_sets="Reactome_2022", organism="human")`
(falls back to the same Enrichr REST endpoints if the package is unavailable), writes
`enrichr_reactome2022_full_results.csv`, prints every p53 / cell-cycle candidate row and names the
primary row; the reported statistic is that row's Enrichr **Odds Ratio** column.

