## Method caveat (important)
Neither R/DESeq2 nor pydeseq2 was provisioned and the sandbox is offline, so DE used the
NumPy/SciPy DESeq2-equivalent in `deseq_equiv.py`. Its GLM matches `statsmodels` NB2 GLM
(log2FC r=0.9935, median SE ratio 0.977), but its normal-reference Wald p-values are mildly
anti-conservative at n=3 vs 3: on simulations the question's threshold combination yields a
~9% false-positive rate among null genes (t(df=4) reference: ~4%). The DE list sizes above should
therefore be read as slightly liberal; `de_symbols_t_df4.txt` is the conservative variant.
